Below is the full plan in 9 phases, written against your current code. For each phase I give what to build, where it goes, how to build it, and what must be true before you move on. I read the file paths below in your zip. Where I say “verify”, I did not read that file closely, so check it before you build on it.

Phase 0: Safety net (half a day)

What: Protect the work you have before you change the access rules.
Where and how:

Create a git branch such as feat/access-v4. Add dist/, .turbo/, *.tsbuildinfo and apps/api/uploads/ to .gitignore. Your zip contains build output that should not be committed.
Pick one Prisma migration folder. You have packages/database/prisma/migrations and prisma/schema/migrations, and two sources of truth will break migrate deploy.
Add a feature flag in apps/mobile/src/core/config/env.ts, for example ACCESS_MODEL=v4. This lets you switch back if something fails in testing.
Mark the old tests as expected to change: downloadsAccess.test.ts and offlineAccess.test.ts.

Done when: The branch builds and tests pass as they do today.

